; RUN: %solver --SMTLIB2 %s | %OutputCheck %s
;
; Two hundred applications at two hundred distinct arguments. Nothing here
; makes any two of them equal, and nothing prunes them either: the arguments
; are unrelated symbols, so every one of the 19 900 pairs might be equal until
; a model says otherwise.
;
; Stating that relation in advance is what does not scale -- each pair is an
; equality atom, and each equality atom is a row and a slack variable in the
; tableau before the search has run once. Deciding it from a committed model
; instead costs one grouping of the applications by their arguments' values,
; and every pair the model already agrees about is never stated at all.
